From: Steffen Jaeckel <sjaeckel@suse.de>
Subject: kABI fix for disabling of CONFIG_CAN.
Patch-mainline: Never, kABI workaround
References: jsc#PED-16993

We must include struct netns_can into struct net in order to preserve kABI.

Signed-off-by: Steffen Jaeckel <sjaeckel@suse.de>
Reviewed-by: Petr Pavlu <petr.pavlu@suse.com>
[mkoutny: drop CONFIG_SUSE_HAVE_STABLE_KABI]
Acked-by: Petr Pavlu <petr.pavlu@suse.com>

---
 include/net/net_namespace.h |    7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/include/net/net_namespace.h
+++ b/include/net/net_namespace.h
@@ -177,7 +177,12 @@ struct net {
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MPLS)
 	struct netns_mpls	mpls;
 #endif
-#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CAN)
+	/* We have disabled CAN, but in order to preserve kABI
+	 * we have to include the struct on the architectures
+	 * where it had been enabled.
+	 */
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CAN) || \
+	(IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_X86_64) || IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARM64))
 	struct netns_can	can;
 #endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_XDP_SOCKETS
